The graph of $y = f(x)$ is shown for $0 \le x \le 5$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$},
  xmin=-0.8, xmax=5.8, ymin=-6, ymax=46, samples=100, clip=false,
  xtick={1,2,3,4,5}, ytick={10,20,30,40}, width=9cm, height=9cm]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:5] {2*x*x*x - 12*x*x + 18*x};
\addplot[only marks, mark=*] coordinates {(0,0) (5,40)};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the global maximum value of $f$ on this domain?
